  "character": "The heart of the Three Valleys. Chalet-architecture, British favourite, excellent intermediates terrain, wooded setting.",
  "description": "M\u00e9ribel is the central resort of the Three Valleys \u2014 literally and spiritually. It occupies the middle valley, giving it the fastest access to all three valleys (Courchevel, Belleville, and M\u00e9ribel itself). Founded by British army officer Peter Lindsay in 1938 and developed with a strict wood-clad, stone-tiled chalet-style architectural policy, it is one of the more attractive purpose-built resorts in the Alps. The wooded setting distinguishes it from the treeless high-altitude resorts. A perennial favourite with British skiers.",
